ices the infrastructure the data  center would be located at their  premises itself let's understand the  definition of a private cloud it says  that the private cloud means using a  cloud infrastructure only for our  dedicated customer or the organization  so you can have a dedicated  infrastructure for your clients or the  organization and that would not be  shared with the other users let's  understand the definition of a hybrid  cloud the hybrid cloud is basically the  combination of the public and the  private clocked it's based on the  purpose and the requirements so here we  are discussing about the hybrid cloud  definition with respect to the cloud  native approach so whenever you discuss  about the cloud native approach you  always discuss about the combination of  a public cloud plus private cloud which  is basically a hybrid cloud now the  company that provides the services only  related to the public cloud is the  global dots so Global dot is one of the  company that offers worldwide public  cloud services whereas the company that  offers the private cloud kind of a  services that means dedicated to a  particular organization or the customer  that is Dell so we know about Dell it is  one of the companies that offer the  private cloud services and in case of a  hybrid cloud services iBM is the company  which offers and the hybrid cloud and  offer services to the customers now  there is one feature in the cloud cloud  deployment models which is called as the  tenancy tenancy is basically kind of a  virtual partitioning of the resources  and all those resources will be kept  isolated so in case of a tenancy in the  case of a public cloud it is basically a  multi tenant kind of a set up in which  data of many organizations probably a  different organization in different  geographies can store the data in a  shared environment since it's a multi  tenant so their data would be completely  isolated to another organizations data  as well now in the tenancy example in  the case of a private cloud would be it  will be only a single tenancy since the  private cloud infrastructure is only  dedicated to a single customer or the  single organization whereas in the case  of a hybrid cloud the tenancy is defined  as the data stored in a public cloud is  multi tenant and it is kept securely as  well as private with the help of a  private cloud so we have a public cloud  and we have a hybrid cloud which offers  us the multi-tenancy unlike in the case  of a private cloud but to make it secure  which was not possible in the case of a  public cloud we use the help of a  private cloud to make it more private  and secure in terms  the data now exposure to public how the  public accesses these cloud models so  the public cloud is accessed by everyone  there are very least restrictions or no  restrictions anyone in any from any  place any geography or any device can  access the services whereas the access  of the private cloud can be only done by  the administrators inside the  organization whereas the case of a  hybrid cloud since it's a combination of  a public plus private cloud so it can be  accessed from by the within the  organization if it you are using it and  in the form of a private cloud kind of a  service or if it's in the kind of a  public cloud service it can be accessed  from any location now the data center  locations where exactly the data center  of these cloud models are situated at so  for the public cloud on the internet  with the cloud service providers are  available there itself the data centers  are so the data center locations for the  public cloud are on the same premises  where the cloud provider is located at  so over the public Internet this data  center or the infrastructure can be  accessed the data center location of a  private cloud would be inside the  organization Network only so it will not  be on the public network or the Internet  it would be within the organization and  the hybrid cloud the data center  location inside the organization for  private cloud services and anywhere on  the internet for the public cloud  services so it's up to the organization  so how they have done the deployment if  it's in the form of a public cloud  deployment it can be accessed over the  Internet if it is in the form of a  private cloud deployment done on the  hybrid model it would be access over a  private probably a dedicated network or  over the network which is limited to a  particular organization now the cloud  service providers with respect to the  public cloud and the cloud service  provider manages service whatever the  organization uses them so this is one of  the features of a public cloud service  providers in case of a private cloud  service providers the organization's  need to have their administrators inside  the organization from where the private  cloud is accessed from and in the case  of a hybrid cloud the organization  operates the private cloud whereas the  cloud service provider manages the  public cloud so it can be that the user  can be outside the organization  using the public cloud or the user has  to be inside the organization to access  the private cloud the hardware  components now in the case of a public  cloud the cloud service provider  provides all the hardware's and ensure  it works properly so nothing has to be  implemented or supplied by the  organization or the client to the cloud  service provider everything would be  provided by the cloud service provider  and that's the reason that basically  those people who don't have their  infrastructure or they basically do not  want to procure the infrastructure it's  the best places for a public cloud since  it's available on the Internet it can be  accessed by anyone if the person is not  an organization if it's not the  organization if it's an individual  person also wants to use the public  cloud is the best place in the case of a  private cloud the organization offers  the hardware so organization says that  this is our specification if we just  want that you should put this particular  infrastructure with that specification  into your premises which we can access  it over the netiquette it or the  internal network and that makes it more  expensive now in the case of a hybrid  cloud the organization provides hardware  for the private cloud whereas the cloud  service provider provides you the  infrastructure if in case you are  accessing it in the form of a public  cloud now moving to the expenses let's  see the comparison of the costing  associated with the different cloud  models now coming to the public cloud  model generally what happens in this  case is the public cloud service  provider provides the infrastructure  applications and they host the  applications on their infrastructure at  their premises they give the access off  for those application and the  infrastructure over the network probably  mostly on the internet and hence it  becomes a cheaper option in terms of  accessing the services using a public  cloud now looking to the private cloud  model costing the hardware and network  has to be provided by the organization  that means the company that is  requesting for the infrastructure and  hence it becomes an expensive for the  clients to work on the private cloud  model now looking into the expenses for  the hybrid cloud model it's basically  the costing is intermediate between the  public and the private since the  organization must provide Hardware a  network for the private cloud if they  wanted to access it as a private  loved model then it becomes bit  expensive whereas if they want to access  it like a public cloud model then the  cloud service provider does all the  installation for the cloud so the cost  becomes moderately fair so the top  companies that are using the public  private and the hybrid cloud let's look  into it the public cloud is primarily  used by Amazon Web Services which is one  of the largest cloud service providers